answers=[f"1. P3 successful objects: {s['P3_SUCCESS_N']}/{len(objects)}.",f"2. Total parts: {len(prs)}.",f"3. Major parts: {s['MAJOR_PART_N']}.",f"4. At least one native executable candidate: {sum(p['native_pass'] and p['execute_pass'] for p in attempted)}/{len(attempted)}. This is not geometry acceptance.",f"5. Strict accepted parts: {len(strict)}/{len(attempted)} ({s['PART_STRICT_ACCEPT_RATE']:.2%}); near-pass: {len(near)}; rejected: {s['PART_REJECT_N']}.",'6. Accepted planned families: '+', '.join(f"{k}: {v['strict_accepted']}/{v['attempted']}" for k,v in family.items() if v['strict_accepted'])+'. Other planned families had zero strict accepts. See tables/family_breakdown.csv; small counts do not establish universal ranking.','7. Curved housings, changing cross sections, openings and disconnected surface fragments exceed the compact fitting hypotheses. Selected-candidate failed strict checks (overlapping counts): '+json.dumps(dict(fail_counts))+'. Per-candidate errors and metrics are retained.','8. No paired whole-object baseline was run, so a significant causal benefit from P3 has not been demonstrated. P3 produced independently addressable geometry with recoverable transforms.','9. X-Part used: 0. No independently confirmed severe truncation plus direct failure was established; open segmentation boundaries alone are insufficient.','10. X-Part benefit: not evaluated; no treated/control examples.',f'11. Full major-part strict assemblies: {len(full)}; exported strict subsets: {len(partial)}. Partial can contain only a small fraction of the source, explicitly recorded.',f"12. Full-only IoU/NCD medians: {median([o['object_iou'] for o in full if 'object_iou' in o])} / {median([o['object_normalized_chamfer'] for o in full if 'object_normalized_chamfer' in o])}. Overall nonempty assembly medians use n={len(metrics)} and must not be mistaken for full-object quality.",f"13. Pseudo pairs: parts={s['PSEUDO_PART_PAIR_N']}, objects={s['PSEUDO_OBJECT_PAIR_N']}. These are reconstructed pseudo supervision, never original design GT.",f"14. CAD-derived exact pairs: parts={s['EXACT_PART_PAIR_N']}, objects={s['EXACT_OBJECT_PAIR_N']}. Partial-object exact pairs retain their partial status.",'15. No demonstrated richer accepted CAD distribution than a simple DeepCAD-style dataset. High source triangle count and dense CAD tessellation are not proof of parametric design complexity.','16. Do not scale to 100. Improve part structure and parameter fitting under the same strict gate first.']
report='# P3 high-detail Mesh2CAD factory V1 Smoke20\n\n'+datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()+'\n\n```json\n'+json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\n```\n\n'+'\n\n'.join(answers)+'\n\n## Method and limits\n\nAll original sources and historical results remained read-only within the recorded integrity scope. The new pipeline uses full source objects and real P3 inference. Source hashes, normalization, inverse transforms, face assignments, features, plans, candidates, reload geometry and failures are retained. Geometry uses 20,000 sampled points and the inherited IoU128 approximate scan-fill protocol; this is not exact solid Boolean IoU. All thresholds are frozen.\n\nLLM planning was performed by the interactive Codex assistant after inspecting per-part geometry summaries, with explicit response maps and prompt hashes. It is a replayable frozen-plan run, not a separately callable unattended LLM service. Numeric dimensions come from deterministic geometry fitting. Plans are hypotheses, not recovered design intent. Eight family labels are available, but the initial emitters only cover bounded extrusion/cuts, loft, radial revolve, primitives and limited component unions; true connected frame graph reconstruction is not implemented. This limitation is material.\n\nStrict CAD parts alone enter training-pair manifests and source assemblies. Near and rejected CAD artifacts remain diagnostic only. Assembly compounds preserve independent solids. Source-frame and canonical-frame outputs are distinguished. No mesh wrappers, embedded source facets, per-triangle solids, invented sheet thicknesses or whole-object bounding-box success claims are used.\n\nExact-pair tessellation uses tighter OCC tolerances; if planar CAD retained the same triangle count, one subdivision is recorded explicitly. More triangles do not imply more design detail. Optional scan-like corruption was omitted.\n\nThe synthetic two-solid assembly fixture is an engineering check only, excluded from all object/part/pair counts. Stage records describe whether source-data assembly actually closed; fixture success must not be described as a successful real-object reconstruction.\n\n## Deliverables\n\nSee tables/object_summary.csv, tables/part_summary.csv, tables/candidate_summary.csv, tables/strict_accepted_parts.json, tables/full_assemblies.json, manifests/pseudo_pairs.json, manifests/exact_pairs.json, visualizations/index.html, scripts/run_pipeline.py and reports/REPRODUCE.md.\n'
report+='\n\n## Audit semantics\n\nGOOD in the initial mesh audit means finite, nondegenerate geometry with no independently established severe missing-surface evidence. It is not a watertightness or complete-part certificate. Watertight parts: '+str(sum(p['watertight'] for p in prs))+'/'+str(len(prs))+'. Disconnected parts: '+str(sum(p['components']>1 for p in prs))+'. Open P3 boundaries were never sufficient to trigger X-Part. Family confidence scores are uncalibrated planning confidence, not estimated acceptance probability.\n\nFailed strict checks on selected candidates (overlapping counts): '+json.dumps(dict(fail_counts))+'. Missing metrics are excluded from these counts. See candidate_summary for execution failures and part result.json for generation failures. The family_breakdown table uses planned families; realized_candidate_family uses actual selected construction types. CAD complexity summary medians and operation counts use strict accepted parts only; UNSUPPORTED_N counts attempted H-family plans.\n'
report+='\nThe per-part prompt.txt is a reconstructed planning-context record from the geometry summary inspected in this conversation, not a separately submitted API prompt. Actual interactive model input also included the conversation and batched tool output. Response maps record the explicit decisions used; no independent unattended LLM inference log is claimed.\n'
(O/'reports/REPORT.md').write_text(report)
cn=f'''# Smoke20 结论\n\n20 个完整高模对象中，P3 成功 {s['P3_SUCCESS_N']} 个，生成 {len(prs)} 个部件，其中主要部件 {s['MAJOR_PART_N']} 个。严格接受 {len(strict)}/{len(attempted)}（{s['PART_STRICT_ACCEPT_RATE']:.2%}），近通过 {len(near)}，拒绝 {s['PART_REJECT_N']}。\n\n完整主要部件装配 {len(full)}/20，非空严格部件子集装配 {len(partial)} 个。所有装配的 IoU/NCD 中位数分别为 {s['OBJECT_IOU_MEDIAN']} / {s['OBJECT_NCD_MEDIAN']}，有效分母 {len(metrics)}。空装配没有可定义的几何误差，不能填零。子集装配不代表大部分物体已恢复。\n\n结论：未证实已获得高保真复杂 CAD 数据，不应扩到 100。下一阶段应改进部件结构推断与参数拟合。程序执行与 STEP 回读成功不等于几何重建成功。没有放宽严格门槛，没有将 near-pass 放入训练配对。\n\nX-Part 使用 0 次：尚无独立证据确认严重缺面是直接重建失败原因。未做全物体基线或 X-Part 对照，不能宣称 P3 或 X-Part 带来显著因果收益。\n\n伪配对：部件 {s['PSEUDO_PART_PAIR_N']}，整物体 {s['PSEUDO_OBJECT_PAIR_N']}；CAD 同源精确配对：部件 {s['EXACT_PART_PAIR_N']}，物体/子集 {s['EXACT_OBJECT_PAIR_N']}。伪 CAD 不是真实原始设计 GT；高精度细分增加三角面数不等于增加设计复杂度。\n\n前三、前五个样本均没有严格件，因此真实物体的端到端装配未闭合；后续 20 个样本仅完成本次限定范围的失败诊断覆盖。合成装配工程测试单独保存，未混入数据成功数。详细 16 问、统计口径与局限见 REPORT.md。\n'''
(O/'reports/SUMMARY_ZH.md').write_text(cn);print(json.dumps(s,indent=2))
